BT /F1 9.5 Tf 48 555.5 Td (By exercise; it must be supplied with nourishment or it cannot live.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 48 533 Td (74. How does imagination differ from day-dreaming?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 48 518 Td (Day-dreaming is a form of mental dissipation, while imagination is a form of constructive) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 48 504.5 Td (thought which must precede every constructive action.) Tj ET
